senses.gloss:
पर-क्षेत्र (त्रं) 1.
n. Another man's wife;
another field; another's body.

परत्र-भीरु (रुः) 2.
m. A pious man;
regarding future rewards, &c.

पर-दार (रः) 1.
m. Another's wife;
adultery, intrigue.

पर-म्पद (दं) 1.
n. Eternal felicity;
Viṣṇu's abode, highest heaven.

परम्परीण (णः-णा-णं)
a. Hereditary;
traditional. Also परम्परागत.

पारक (कः-का-की-कं)
a. Purifying;
cherishing; conducting across.

परा-क्रम (मः) 1.
m. Power; exertion;
valour; going forth; attack.

परा_ङ्मुख (खः-खा-खं)
a. Turning away;
having the face averted.

परा-मृष्ट (ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)
p. Considered;
touched by; endured.

परा-वर्त्त्य (र्त्त्यः-र्त्त्या-र्त्त्यं)
a. Exchange;
turned back; reversed.

परा-वृत्त (त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)
p. Fled; turned;
reversed; changed; restored.

परी_क्षा (क्षा) 1.
f. Discrimination;
test, trial; temptation.

परि-क्षेप (पः) 1.
m. A scattering;
surrounding; leaving.

परि-गम (मः) 1.
m. Surrounding;
seeking; knowing; getting.

परि-गृहीत (तः-ता-तं)
p. Received;
assented to; obeyed; checked.

परि-चय (यः) 1.
m. Acquaintance;
meeting a friend; accumulation.

परि-चाय्य (य्यः) 1.
m. Sacrificial fire;
its place; raising the rent of land.

परि-च्छद (दः) 1.
m. Court; train;
family; property; dress.

परि-च्छन्न (न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)
p. Covered;
invested; having a train.

परि-च्छिन्न (न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)
p. Cut off;
resisted; remedied.

परि-णाय (यः) 1.
m. Leading round;
moving a piece at chess.

परि-णिंसक (कः-का-कं)
a. Kissing;
eating, feeding upon.

परि-ताप (पः) 1.
m. Pain; sorrow;
heat; fear; division of hell.

परि-त्राण (णं) 1.
n. Warding a blow;
deliverance, salvation.

परि-पक्व (क्वः-क्वा-क्वं)
a. Ripe; cooked;
shrewd; digested.

परि-भाषण (णं) 1.
n. Reproof, ridicule;
converse; agreement; rule.

परि-मृदित (तः-ता-तं)
p. Rubbed;
embraced, invested; spread.

परी-वाद (दः) 1.
m. Reproof, abuse;
quill, or bow of a lute.

परि-वाह (हः) 1.
m. An inundation;
a water-course.

परिवृत (तः-ता-तं)
p. Surrounded;
gained; received entirely; known.

परि-वेषण (णं) 1.
n. Surrounding;
serving out a meal to guests.

परि-वेष्टित (तः-ता-तं)
a. Enclosed;
surrounded; covered, veiled.

परि-ष्कार (रः) 1.
m. Decoration;
polishing; purifying; cooking;
surrounding.

परि-सर्य्या (र्य्या) 1.
f. Perambulation;
near approach; service.

परि-स्पन्दमान (नः-ना-नं)
a. Throbbing;
moving; shaking, quivering.

परि-हित (तः-ता-तं)
p. Placed on;
covered; invested.

परी-ष्टि (ष्टिः) 2.
f. Enquiry, research;
service; willingness.

पर्ज्जन्य (न्यः) 1.
m. Indra; cloud;
thunder cloud; distant thunder.

पर्ण-नर (रः) 1.
m. A man of leaves;
effigy of one dead and lost.

पर्प (र्पं) 1.
n. A house; young grass;
a wheel chair for invalid.

पर्य्या_य (यः) 1.
m. Order; method;
manner; occasion; meaning.

पर्य्य_स्त (स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)
a. Fallen; struck;
upset; dismissed; bowed down.

पर्य्या_प्ति (प्तिः) 2.
f. Willingness;
obtaining; satisfaction; entire-
[]
ness; adequacy; discrimination;
guarding against.

पर्य्या_हार (रः) 1.
n. A taking; a load;
a yoke; a store; a pitcher.

पारशीक (कः) 1.
m. Persia; a Persian;
a Persian horse.

पारियानिक (कः) 1.
m. A travelling;
conveyance, cart or carriage.

पार्थ (र्थः) 1.
m. A king;
Arjuna;
Mars; a tree (Pentaptera arjuna.)

पार्व्वा-यना-न्तीय (यः-या-यं)
a. Of the
end of a feast day (a sacrifice.)

पार्ष्णि (र्ष्णिः) 2.
m. f. The heel; rear
of an army; the back; a kick;
asking.
f. Violent woman;
Kuntī.
